Boot and reboot recovery
------------------------
Cold cycle at 2026-10-14T09:25:14Z used the saved relay channel and 1000 ms off interval.
Serial COM18 showed dshanpi-axcl.service finish successfully and reached the login prompt in 27.2 s.
After boot, systemctl reported the service enabled and active, axcl-smi returned 0, the NPU suite
again passed 20/20, and there were no firmware-load or heartbeat-timeout messages.

Following the final reinstall of 2026.10.14-1, systemctl reboot took the board down after 2 s.
SSH returned after 18 s. The release marker was 2026.10.14-1, the AXCL service was enabled and
active, axcl-smi returned 0 at 45 C, and the NPU suite again passed 20/20. systemctl --failed and
dpkg --audit produced no output; the current boot contained no firmware-load or heartbeat timeout.

AIC8800D80 acceptance
---------------------
After reboot, aic_load_fw, aic8800_fdrv and aic_btusb loaded automatically. The Wi-Fi interface
returned, scanned successfully, connected through NetworkManager, obtained 192.168.1.12/24, resolved
DNS and downloaded the public release manifest over HTTPS. Network names and credentials are omitted.

BlueZ was active. bluetoothctl reported the AIC controller powered with central and peripheral roles.
A bounded discovery scan returned 0 and found five devices; names and addresses are omitted. Pairable
and discovery were returned to off after the scan.

Rollback and reinstall
----------------------
The first noninteractive rollback attempt stopped at APT confirmation and changed no packages. The
operator then supplied one explicit confirmation. dspi-config rollback returned 0 and installed
dshanpi-a1-release-core 2026.10.10-1 while preserving the exact AXCL selector and package cohort.
A cold reboot completed, dshanpi-axcl.service finished, axcl-smi returned 0 at 46 C, and dpkg --audit
was empty. dspi-config then installed 2026.10.14-1 again; the final reboot and AXCL/NPU checks above
passed. This records both the safe failure branch and the completed rollback/reinstall path.

Scope
-----
This acceptance covers the release lock, AIC Wi-Fi and Bluetooth discovery, AXCL runtime/PAC/DKMS,
reboot recovery and the supplied NPU unit suite. Bluetooth pairing/transfer, sustained inference,
multi-stream throughput and long-duration thermal soak were not part of this stable gate.
